1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,544
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:04,963
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,466 --> 00:00:10,552
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:12,679
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:16,224
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,561
[squeals, in Visayan] Oh my God! This kid!

7
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,354
You're my daddy's maid, right?

8
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:23,231
- I'm an assistant.
- [quirky sting]

9
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:25,108
That's the same thing.
What's wrong with you?

10
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:26,401
[Tonet] <i>AB positive?</i>

11
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:28,361
So, that child has blue blood.

12
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,363
- Tatoy, your coffee.
- Ibyang.

13
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,532
[Janine] <i>Daddy, I also know</i>
<i>how to make coffee.</i>

14
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:35,493
<i>It's tastier than what Ibyang made.</i>

15
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,370
[retches]

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,289
[Atoy] Ugh! It tastes salty.

17
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:44,210
[Atoy] <i>Ibyang, I want you</i>
<i>to make peace with Janine, okay?</i>

18
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,879
I want you to apologize to her.

19
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:48,089
[Atoy] <i>You? You can donate too.</i>

20
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:49,340
<i>You definitely can.</i>

21
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,633
What's your type?

22
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,302
You.

23
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:53,595
[Janine] <i>I'll try this on.</i>

24
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:56,097
- [Ibyang] <i>Hey! Don't go in there!</i>
- [Janine mutters]

25
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:57,015
[Ibyang] <i>We can't!</i>

26
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:57,974
PREVIOUSLY

27
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,142
[Ibyang] <i>Put that back.</i>

28
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,478
[Janine] You're the troublemaker. What?!

29
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:03,897
[indistinct chatter]

30
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,023
[Denden] <i>My phone!</i>

31
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,983
[Emerson] <i>You just walked straight, huh.</i>

32
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,610
- [Emerson] That's it, that's it!
- Thank you.

33
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:09,944
- [Emerson grunts, groans]
- [Denden squeals]

34
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,404
- [Emerson gasps]
- [people clamor]

35
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:14,199
Wait. What are you doing outside?
Why are you here?

36
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:15,450
Ibyang sent me out.

37
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,619
[Atoy] <i>I told her not to fight with you.</i>
<i>Where is she?</i>

38
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:20,455
[Janine] <i>She's in that… secret room.</i>

39
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:22,373
You're not supposed to go in there.
Get out of here!

40
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:25,210
[Ibyang sobs]

41
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:29,631
[music fades]

42
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:34,260
[Ibyang sobbing]

43
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:42,268
[Tonet] What did you do to Ibyang?!

44
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:44,562
- [Ibyang sobs]
- Did you hurt Ibyang?

45
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,648
Why would I hurt her?

46
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:48,399
[Tonet] Then…

47
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,985
Then why are you putting ice on your hand?

48
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:52,779
What happened?

49
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,156
Ah, no.

50
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,908
I just got into trouble at the court.

51
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,034
There was…

52
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,370
Anyway, it's a long story.

53
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,539
But on my way home,

54
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:06,960
I saw… Ibyang outside, crying.

55
00:02:07,043 --> 00:02:09,337
She wouldn't say why.

56
00:02:10,046 --> 00:02:11,464
So, I brought her along.

57
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:17,095
Then I told Atoy that Ibyang was here,
so he wouldn't worry.

58
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:19,764
- [Ibyang sniffles]
- [Tonet sighs]

59
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,307
Come drink some water.

60
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:22,892
Stop crying now.

61
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:23,810
‪[gentle music playing]

62
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,067
Ibyang,

63
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:35,280
you know you can talk to Sis Tonet, right?

64
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,448
Why are you crying?

65
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:41,619
Tatoy got mad at me.

66
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:45,957
Uh, why? Did you do something wrong?

67
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:49,669
It was Janine's fault.

68
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:54,090
But I was the one scolded.

69
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:04,726
Don't worry.

70
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,144
I'll take care of you.

71
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:11,774
Of all things I dislike,
seeing you cry is the worst.

72
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:14,068
Because you know,

73
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:17,238
I love you so much.

74
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:20,742
[Tonet] Mmm?

75
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:22,243
Why are you crying?

76
00:03:22,327 --> 00:03:24,829
This child is so frustrating.

77
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,748
You're making me cry too.

78
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:28,124
Don't cry anymore.

79
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:33,963
I'm not used to hearing
someone say they love me.

80
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:39,302
Only Sis Ame and Tatoy said that to me.

81
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:43,473
But it's one less now because of Janine.

82
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:45,642
[sniffs]

83
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:48,144
Atoy still loves you.

84
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,521
That won't change.

85
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:54,776
But he'll answer to me.

86
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:59,697
Just because he's my TTH
doesn't mean he'll escape my temper.

87
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:02,992
I love you too, Sis Tonet.

88
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,170
[suave theme music playing]

89
00:04:41,155 --> 00:04:42,198
The manual is here.

90
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,951
If you want to change
the code of your smart lock.

91
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:46,619
All right, here it is.

92
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,787
Thanks.

93
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:49,455
Good thing you're available even at night.

94
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:51,541
This can't wait.

95
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:55,044
The kids got into that room twice already.

96
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:59,424
That can't happen.
There weren't kids here before.

97
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:00,466
Thank you.

98
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:03,970
You've helped me a lot more, Atoy.
This is a small thing.

99
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:07,348
If you have a problem, call me.

100
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,975
- I'll go ahead.
- Okay, bro.

101
00:05:09,058 --> 00:05:10,518
- All right, bro.
- [Atoy] Okay.

102
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,073
[knocking on door]

103
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:27,702
[pensive music playing]

104
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:39,130
[tense stinging]

105
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:41,966
Oh, why?

106
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:43,593
Is there a problem?

107
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:44,802
[in Visayan] Yes.

108
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:46,971
You're not fair.

109
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:48,306
Huh?

110
00:05:48,389 --> 00:05:49,640
[Tonet huffs]

111
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:53,561
Ibyang is at my brother's shop.
She's still crying.

112
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:56,814
[dramatic sting]

113
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,733
Of course. I scolded her!

114
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,860
I warned her. She didn't listen to me.

115
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,820
That's the thing!

116
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:05,323
She only obeyed what you wanted.

117
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,408
And she's still the one at fault?

118
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:08,910
Huh?

119
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:12,997
She just stopped your bratty daughter!

120
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:16,125
Hey, don't talk about
my daughter like that.

121
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,129
But it's true!
And now you're siding with Janine?

122
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,130
[pensive music playing]

123
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:25,718
Of course, I'm just doing
my responsibility as a father.

124
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:26,969
Father?

125
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:30,139
Father of who? Of your child?

126
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,766
What about Ibyang?

127
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,893
I feel bad for that child.

128
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,978
If you don't want her, say so!

129
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:39,315
Don't make her feel worthless!

130
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:40,983
Be fair, Atoy!

131
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:46,989
[dramatic sting]

132
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:08,219
[muffled chattering in the distance]

133
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:09,345
[Emerson clears throat]

134
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:14,183
- [Emerson] I'll leave you for now.
- Thanks, bro.

135
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,268
[Emerson] Mmm-mmm.

136
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:17,812
[Atoy clears throat]

137
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,460
‪[light tapping on table]

138
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:45,339
Sorry if I scolded you.

139
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:47,049
[Atoy inhales]

140
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,259
[Atoy] The truth is…

141
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:50,595
I was scared.

142
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:55,183
I was nervous for you.
What if something happened to you?

143
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,101
To both of you!

144
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:00,271
That's what I was thinking too.

145
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:03,274
That's why I stopped Janine.

146
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,903
But you got mad at me.

147
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,906
I didn't do anything wrong.

148
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:12,992
[Atoy sighs]

149
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:17,872
What I want is for you
to be more responsible.

150
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:20,291
Of course, you're the older sister.

151
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,586
[gentle music playing]

152
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:24,629
Older sister?

153
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:27,840
Yes, older sister.

154
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:31,177
We've been together longer, right?

155
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,263
So, for me, you're the eldest.

156
00:08:35,139 --> 00:08:36,265
You're the older sister.

157
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:41,854
So that means
you should show her what's right.

158
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,189
She'll follow you,

159
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:46,859
and if she does something wrong,
if she doesn't listen to you,

160
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:49,570
if you see her doing something bad,

161
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:51,322
you are to tell me.

162
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,241
Can we do that?

163
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:56,369
[Atoy sighs]

164
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:04,085
Ibyang, we're one family now.

165
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:06,963
I'm the father,

166
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:10,508
and you and Janine are both my children.

167
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:14,011
But I want you to get along.

168
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,974
Well, it's normal for siblings to fight.

169
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:19,517
That's natural.

170
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,893
But who knows?

171
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:23,729
Maybe you'll even become best friends.

172
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:26,065
Right?

173
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:28,693
Mmm-hmm?

174
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:31,612
Let's go home, Tatoy.

175
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:34,156
I'll try again

176
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,576
for Janine and me to be sisters.

177
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,078
Very good. Come here!

178
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,122
Come here. Come, come.

179
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,790
[sentimental music playing]

180
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,302
Do you want dumplings?

181
00:09:55,511 --> 00:09:56,470
Let's go.

182
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:10,818
Janine, you didn't tell me
the truth earlier.

183
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:13,613
Uh, was really
kicked out by Ibyang though.

184
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:14,572
[Atoy] Even so.

185
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:16,741
You still didn't tell me the reason.

186
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:20,328
Ibyang already forbade you,
but you still did it.

187
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,415
[inaudible] Tattletale, tattletale!

188
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:25,625
[Atoy] Psst, hey.

189
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:29,003
Enough of that, okay. Enough!

190
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:32,923
When I say enough, it's over.

191
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,508
I don't want that to happen again.

192
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:38,054
There's a reason
I forbid you from doing that.

193
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,639
It's for your own good.

194
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,682
Do you understand?
I don't want that to happen again.

195
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,267
- Is that clear?
- [inaudible]

196
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:44,352
[mellow music playing]

197
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,020
- [Atoy] Is it clear?
- Yes, Dad.

198
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,396
[in English] Yes.

199
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:52,652
All right then.

200
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,570
You both go to sleep now.

201
00:10:55,071 --> 00:10:56,864
Tomorrow…

202
00:10:57,531 --> 00:10:59,742
[clicks tongue] I'll take you both out!

203
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:02,119
- [pleasant music playing]
- [gasps]

204
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,829
Where are we going?

205
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,998
[Atoy] It's a secret.

206
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,166
Go, go to sleep now.

207
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:09,543
No more fighting, okay, Ibyang?

208
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:12,546
[Atoy] Okay?

209
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,384
[smooches]

210
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:24,767
Hey.

211
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,603
I'll have this bed for myself.

212
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,397
You sleep on the floor.

213
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,776
[pensive music playing]

214
00:11:33,859 --> 00:11:37,113
[grunts] All right,
I'll sleep here instead.

215
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:42,118
Tatoy might get mad if we fight again.

216
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:45,204
Good night, Janine.

217
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:50,793
Why did you even come back?
You're not the real child.

218
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:53,254
[pensive music playing]

219
00:11:56,340 --> 00:12:01,720
‪[dramatic stinging]

220
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:04,223
‪[dramatic sting]

221
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:13,023
Atoy? Ame? Ibyang?

222
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:14,567
- Boo!
- [Tonet squeals]

223
00:12:14,650 --> 00:12:15,860
- [sneaky music playing]
- [Ame chuckles]

224
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:18,237
[in Visayan] This woman's
driving me crazy! [inhales]

225
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,530
[Tonet sighs]

226
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:21,866
Ame, I almost died from shock.

227
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:24,952
Oh, no. I don't want you to die!

228
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,829
You won't see it when Atoy
and I become a couple.

229
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,497
- I'm telling you.
- Oh.

230
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:30,958
What about your dreams?

231
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:32,793
Ah, they're higher than you, like this.

232
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:33,711
- [Ame] Hmm?
- Yes.

233
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:37,673
But with Atoy, yes, let's lower it a bit.

234
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:38,966
Here, yes.

235
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:42,136
Because it really seems… impossible.

236
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,513
Where are they? Where's Atoy, my love?

237
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,973
Where's Miss Cita?

238
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:48,309
Well, Miss Cita is at the court.

239
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:50,811
It's the second day
of the blood donation drive.

240
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:54,273
Atoy and the kids left early.
They said they'd go out.

241
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,609
Actually, I waited for you.

242
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:01,822
To give you this!

243
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,492
What's this? A bribe?

244
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:06,035
It's my thank you gift for you!

245
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:06,952
[bright music playing]

246
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:11,499
Because Ibyang told me
you defended her from Atoy last night.

247
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:14,919
And that you're one
of the people who love her.

248
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,463
It's nothing.

249
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:22,384
It means a lot to Ibyang.
Especially to me.

250
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:24,762
Because what if I'm suddenly gone?

251
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:27,765
You're exaggerating about that!

252
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,518
No one's going anywhere.

253
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,186
We're still far from that.

254
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:35,272
We're still far from
the end of the thread!

255
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:38,609
It's too early for a dramatic moment.

256
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:44,698
But Tonet, I'm grateful for our friendship

257
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:47,535
that's like a light switch.

258
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,079
[both, in English] On and off!

259
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:51,705
[both giggle]

260
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,671
[bright music playing]

261
00:13:59,296 --> 00:14:01,340
Oh? What's this?

262
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:04,426
I thought it was too early for drama?

263
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:09,848
But Tonet…

264
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:14,186
I just want you to know…

265
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,688
[sobs]

266
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:17,439
I already know that!

267
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:21,151
That I'm your best friend
you never expected.

268
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:25,573
That you have a suit to deliver
to Quezon City,

269
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:27,283
to Sir Ralph Torres.

270
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,702
Atoy said you already know where it is.

271
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:32,329
- [sneaky music playing]
- Hmm?

272
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,125
- [Ame] Hurry up…
- [Tonet] Is this it?

273
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:37,626
- Looks like it, right?
- Best friend!

274
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,712
When you get back, we'll eat dumplings.

275
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,089
I'll go now, okay.

276
00:14:42,172 --> 00:14:43,799
- Best friend, love you.
- Best friend!

277
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:50,681
- [Audrey] Tonet, hi!
- Oh!

278
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:51,891
- [Audrey] Um, I'll pick up
- Audrey!

279
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:53,142
Janine.

280
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:54,476
Is she awake?

281
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:56,020
[Tonet] Oh!

282
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,688
They left.

283
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:01,025
Atoy took the kids out.
Didn't he tell you?

284
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:04,737
Um, I didn't say I'd pick her up today.

285
00:15:05,654 --> 00:15:07,114
Um, by the way,

286
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:10,034
how's…

287
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:13,871
Janine? Was there a problem?

288
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:17,124
Ah, none really.

289
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:20,544
I know my daughter has an attitude.

290
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:23,797
So, if she did something
or said something unpleasant,

291
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:27,051
I apologize on her behalf.

292
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:32,222
Honestly, her personality
is really different from you and Atoy.

293
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:35,351
She didn't grow up with us.

294
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,646
But even though she's like that,

295
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:41,065
Janine is my flesh and blood…

296
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,901
and I love my daughter very much.

297
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:46,737
[pensive music playing]

298
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,406
Uh… speaking of blood,

299
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,783
there's…

300
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:53,202
a donation drive at the court now.

301
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:55,371
While you're waiting for Atoy,
you can donate.

302
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:57,706
- [Audrey] Oh…
- [Tonet] Uh…

303
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,626
Don't be scared.
It doesn't hurt. Not at all.

304
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:03,045
And you'll help others too, right?

305
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:06,674
Who knows, someone might need
your blood type.

306
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:08,008
What's your blood type?

307
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,594
[in English] Um, O positive.

308
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:11,971
Just a common blood type.

309
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:13,389
[suspicious music playing]

310
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,766
[Tonet] AB positive?

311
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:17,559
So that child has royal blood.

312
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,104
No wonder she acts like…

313
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,939
a snooty princess.

314
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,482
[Siony] O positive!

315
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,609
You're the same as Atoy!

316
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,820
You're the same. That's good.

317
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:28,821
You can donate now.

318
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:29,822
See, we're the same,

319
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,949
Atoy and I.

320
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:34,743
But hers isn't common.

321
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:36,745
Uh, what did you say?

322
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:39,873
Ah, no!

323
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,000
[tense music playing]

324
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:43,419
I have to go. I'm in a hurry.

325
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:45,337
I need to attend to something.

326
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,505
- Okay, okay!
- [Audrey] Oh, all right.

327
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:47,881
[Audrey] Thanks, Tonet.

328
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:04,690
- Atoy doesn't want his things touched.
- [gasps]

329
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,774
[sneaky music playing]

330
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:09,486
Um… sorry. Ah, I was just curious.

331
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,196
Have a drink first.

332
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,039
It doesn't have poison in it.

333
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:22,416
Thank you.

334
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,503
Uh, do you know

335
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:28,714
what time they'll be back?

336
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:31,383
[quirky stinging]

337
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:35,179
I'll just call Atoy.

338
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:41,351
[line rings]

339
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:44,730
[phone ringing and vibrating]

340
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:50,110
[line ringing]

341
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,991
[Audrey] He really left his phone behind.

342
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:02,122
Actually, Atoy deliberately
left his phone.

343
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:05,000
So he could focus on the two kids

344
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:10,130
without work calls or other distractions.

345
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:13,550
[in English] Okay.

346
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:22,476
- There!
- What game is that, Daddy?

347
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:23,811
This is hopscotch.

348
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:26,980
We played this in the ‘90s…

349
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:29,024
when we were kids in the street.

350
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,485
So, you'll need a stone, okay?

351
00:18:31,568 --> 00:18:34,071
Then you'll place the stone
inside the box.

352
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:36,406
Skip that one. You'll jump, step by step,

353
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:39,493
like… kangaroos.

354
00:18:39,576 --> 00:18:40,911
Oh, get some stones, quick.

355
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:43,664
[light music playing]

356
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:49,795
Oh, Janine, follow me, okay.

357
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:51,046
[Ibyang] I'll do it!

358
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:55,801
All right, put it there.

359
00:18:56,301 --> 00:18:59,221
Then, this first box, skip it.

360
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:00,722
Follow me, okay, oh.

361
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,641
Then two, one.

362
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,394
One, one.

363
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:07,146
[in English] Base!

364
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:09,273
Let's go back. Okay, go. Faster.

365
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:12,693
Two. Oh, oh, oh.

366
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:14,862
[chuckles] Easy, right?

367
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:16,780
[teenager] Brother, brother!

368
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,407
- Let me take a picture of you.
- Oh, sure.

369
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,783
[teenager] You look so cute
as father and child.

370
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,243
You even look alike.

371
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:23,245
Brother? Hello?

372
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:25,455
I'm his real daughter, not her.

373
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:28,167
Oh, is that so? I'm sorry. Okay.

374
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:29,585
[teenager] Here.

375
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,754
[in English] One, two, three.

376
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,882
There! Thank you.

377
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:38,093
Janine, did you really have to say that?

378
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:40,804
I was just telling the truth.

379
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:45,642
Oh, why does it feel like it's my fault?

380
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:47,269
[Atoy] Enough of that, okay.

381
00:19:47,352 --> 00:19:49,396
Enough. Oh, Janine, your turn.
You go next.

382
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:52,316
Daddy, it's so hot here.
I feel like I'm going to melt.

383
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,525
Wow.

384
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,944
You act like you grew up with aircon.

385
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:57,154
[whimsical music playing]

386
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,615
Okay. Where-- Where do you want to go?

387
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:01,909
Anywhere cold!

388
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:05,329
I know, Daddy! Let's go there. Hurry!

389
00:20:08,957 --> 00:20:12,294
Do you know… where they went?

390
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:16,298
Don't you trust Atoy?

391
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:19,843
If there's anyone who's the safest
to be with your child,

392
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:23,388
it's Atoy. Better than ten bodyguards.

393
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:27,893
[sneaky music playing]

394
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:29,186
I know that.

395
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,855
But I wish he brought his phone,

396
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:35,108
so I'd know what's happening
with my child, right?

397
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:39,863
[in English] Ms. Audrey, relax.

398
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:43,200
Let Atoy spend time with his kids.

399
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:46,119
Isn't this his time with Janine?

400
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:47,913
So, just give it to him.

401
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:51,750
[in English] You're right.

402
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:55,712
BE A HERO
DONATE BLOOD TODAY

403
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,881
What's the blood type again?

404
00:20:57,965 --> 00:20:59,633
Ah, that?

405
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:04,846
I know the mother and father
are both O positive,

406
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:08,183
but their child is AB positive.

407
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,143
- Is that possible?
- Oh, no.

408
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:12,145
That's impossible.

409
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:13,063
[dramatic sting]

410
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,064
So…

411
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:17,359
So, Janine isn't Atoy's child?

412
00:21:17,442 --> 00:21:19,778
[tense music playing]

413
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:23,156
Ah, miss, can you please explain to me?

414
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,450
Make it simple to understand.

415
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:31,415
Why it's not possible to have a child
whose blood type is AB

416
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:34,042
when the mother and father are both O.

417
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:35,711
Here's how it works, miss.

418
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:40,757
A child with blood type AB
must inherit one A allele

419
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,634
from one parent

420
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:45,345
and one B allele from the other.

421
00:21:45,846 --> 00:21:51,727
Now, if both parents are type O,
they cannot pass on A or B.

422
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:54,313
Perfect explanation.

423
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:57,941
I just really needed to know,
because they might not believe me

424
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,776
that Janine isn't their child.

425
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:03,780
But miss, don't make the blood type
as the sole basis.

426
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:07,492
Because there can be human error
in blood group reporting.

427
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:12,247
Better yet, retest
the parents and the child

428
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,333
for accurate blood typing.

429
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:17,711
It's also best to do
paternity and maternity tests

430
00:22:17,794 --> 00:22:19,046
for the child.

431
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:21,423
Audrey!

432
00:22:21,506 --> 00:22:23,800
You're amazing-- Ouch.
You're amazing, miss.

433
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:26,511
That's right. Audrey.
Oh, is this okay now?

434
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:27,512
- Can I leave?
- [nurse] Ah, wait.

435
00:22:27,596 --> 00:22:30,223
- [nurse] Just a moment.
- [Tonet] Ah, not yet? Sorry.

436
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:31,308
[in English] Sorry.

437
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:33,602
[rock music playing]

438
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:35,937
[Red] Thank you.

439
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:42,319
[mysterious music playing]

440
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:43,320
[Martina, in English] Hi, hon.

441
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:47,115
So, the maid just told me
Audrey brought Janine to Atoy's place

442
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:48,742
to spend the weekend there.

443
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:50,494
Did you know that?

444
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,371
Now I know. And?

445
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:55,248
[in English] Oh my God.

446
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:59,336
Hasn't your coffee kicked in yet?
Be nervous at least a little.

447
00:23:00,378 --> 00:23:02,589
Why should I be nervous?
I'm not afraid of Atoy.

448
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:05,550
[in English] That's not what I mean.

449
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,761
Isn't it unsettling that Atoy
has been with Janine

450
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:09,346
for that long?

451
00:23:09,429 --> 00:23:12,641
What if he notices
or finds out that the child isn't his?

452
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:18,688
You know, Audrey and Atoy are so excited
about their "child".

453
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:22,651
They'll only think Janine isn't theirs
if someone gives them the idea,

454
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:26,613
which won't happen.
Because only we know the truth, right?

455
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:28,698
[tense music playing]

456
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:29,616
[in English] Relax.

457
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:51,304
[Tonet pants]

458
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:52,430
[Tonet] Audrey!

459
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:54,975
[panting] Oh, Ame!

460
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:57,185
Why did you let Audrey leave?

461
00:23:57,269 --> 00:24:00,021
[Ame] No, she decided to leave.

462
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:03,900
She even said she'd just
pick up Janine tomorrow.

463
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:06,069
So, where's Atoy now?

464
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:07,696
Ah, at the park.

465
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:10,115
I didn't tell Audrey where they were,

466
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:12,367
so she'd stop bothering Atoy.

467
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:15,287
Oh, then I'll deliver this later, okay.

468
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:18,832
Because right now, I need to talk to Atoy.

469
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:19,875
Wait.

470
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,084
[rousing music playing]

471
00:24:31,511 --> 00:24:35,223
- [security] What do you need?
- I know Audrey Regalia.

472
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:38,476
[Tonet] <i>I just want to talk to her.</i>
<i>It's important.</i>

473
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:42,022
But, I'm-- I'm family. She's my niece,
so, she's also my concern.

474
00:24:42,606 --> 00:24:45,317
Did Audrey have Janine DNA-tested?

475
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:48,653
[in English] Are you saying that Janine
is not really their child?

476
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:51,406
You've asked Tatoy for so much already!

477
00:24:51,489 --> 00:24:53,658
He might go broke because of you!

478
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:56,203
Daddy can handle it.
He has a lot of money.

479
00:24:56,786 --> 00:24:57,954
You're such a meddler, aren't you?

480
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:58,788
UP NEXT

481
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:02,334
- Meddler!
- [grunting]

482
00:25:02,417 --> 00:25:03,668
- [man] I'll kill you, bro!
- [Emerson screaming]

483
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:05,045
[old woman] <i>Twice…</i>

484
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:05,921
[Emerson screams]

485
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:10,592
<i>…escaped death.</i>
<i>On the third, it will be final.</i>

486
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:15,639
If not you, then someone you love.

487
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:17,599
Send your men to follow that woman.

488
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:19,893
[Red] <i>Don't let her get near Atoy.</i>

489
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:22,270
If she resists, you know what to do.

490
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:23,521
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

491
00:25:23,605 --> 00:25:24,439
[in English] Yes, boss.

492
00:25:24,522 --> 00:25:25,565
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

493
00:25:26,149 --> 00:25:28,735
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

494
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:31,029
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

495
00:25:31,112 --> 00:25:32,447
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
